**Why B1 is expected:** every `setAlarm` this code performs sets A := the then-minimum pending `due_at` (or now + 10 min on an empty schedule). Pending rows are removed or rescheduled only inside alarm processing (`alarm()` marks rows done / backs them off; `_voidDispatch` voids a grant's lease row — itself alarm- or drain-invoked). No alarm processing is recorded after A was set, and all post-A `_schedule` insertions are future-dated relative to their insertion time (lease +15 min, retry +30 s, watchdog +10 min), so none can undercut A. The single platform alarm is not "for" a row in any case (D1: one alarm per DO) — A is simply the timestamp the platform was last told; B1 says the schedule and the platform value still agree, and delivery is what is missing.

